{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017202-ephemera-to-create-elements","id":1017202,"title":"Ephemera to create elements?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T12:16:48-08:00","id":1017202,"title":"Ephemera to create elements?","content":"So i was going through Dark Ages: Mage and i noticed a foci with a neat ability: it could spend a point of quintessence to create a torch flame at the tip of a staff by attracting tiny fire spirits (they are described as fireflies for those who could see them). this got me to thinking: in m20, leaving aside questions of paradox for a minute, could one use ephemera, or tiny local spirits to manifest energies such as fire. if so would this be penalized by the gauntlet, or are there other limitations i haven't thought of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:40:55-08:00","id":1017216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017202-ephemera-to-create-elements#post1017202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i was going through Dark Ages: Mage and i noticed a foci with a neat ability: it could spend a point of quintessence to create a torch flame at the tip of a staff by attracting tiny fire spirits (they are described as fireflies for those who could see them). this got me to thinking: in m20, leaving aside questions of paradox for a minute, could one use ephemera, or tiny local spirits to manifest energies such as fire. if so would this be penalized by the gauntlet, or are there other limitations i haven't thought of?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it would be Spirit 3 with Forces 3 to turn ephemera into forces, but it might be Spirit 4. Yes you would be hampered by the gauntlet, and you'd better hope that spirit doesn't mind being turned into fire, because otherwise you're probably going to get burned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:58:01-08:00","id":1017237,"title":"","content":"hmm... ah okay so i had to double check How Do You Do That? and it Does mention conjuring spiritual elements from ephemera. it mentions this as being flavor for spirit 2, but actually doable for spirit 3, however it isn't quite clear whether it requires forces to do so, i think it does.... anyway my take on it is that you can substitute spirit 3 for prime 2 to conjure an element if there would be appropriate ephemera in the umbra (i suppose hypothetically you could conjure it from an elemental plane though i could forsee problems arising from that) and spirit 5 would let you create the element from ephemera","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:10:48-08:00","id":1017307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017202-ephemera-to-create-elements?p=1017237#post1017237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm... ah okay so i had to double check How Do You Do That? and it Does mention conjuring spiritual elements from ephemera. it mentions this as being flavor for spirit 2, but actually doable for spirit 3, however it isn't quite clear whether it requires forces to do so, i think it does.... anyway my take on it is that you can substitute spirit 3 for prime 2 to conjure an element if there would be appropriate ephemera in the umbra (i suppose hypothetically you could conjure it from an elemental plane though i could forsee problems arising from that) and spirit 5 would let you create the element from ephemera</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading in Book of Worlds or Infinite Tapestry (maybe both?) that when you're in the Umbra, especially the middle umbra, you can use Spirit magic in similar ways as you would use Matter on inert ephemera and Life on living ephemera, also known as spirits. How Forces fits into this is a bit less certain, because arguably anything that could be considered a Force in the mundane world, is actually a sentient spirit of some description in the umbra. This means that you Spirit 3 can be used to heal and harm spirits, and sculpt or disintegrate spiritual objects, and Spirit 4 can be used to reshape spirits and fused spiritual objects together or pull of &quot;Break Reality&quot; style effects.<br /> <br /> However, if you're doing anything with spirits in the mundane world. You need Spirit simply to interact with the gauntlet enough to touch them, let alone manipulate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T18:22:06-08:00","id":1017422,"title":"","content":"Cutting across the various editions (and taking the aggregate truth among them, as essentially represented in M:20), you *can* use just Spirit:2 to <i>tangentially </i>manifest a (F)orces effect by way of calling upon a spirit to come and perform &quot;x&quot; ability that they inherently possess. The nuances involved, though, are where things get complicated. The spirit in question must be &quot;awake&quot;, somewhere relatively nearby (or the time must be allowed for it to makes its way to the mage... which can be quite some time for some spirits...), and it must have the ability (on its own) to manifest &quot;x&quot; into the physical world, directly (a quality which a great many spirits *dont'* have the ability to do, even when they are embodiments of &quot;x&quot; quality). That type of example was given in Sorcerers Crusade, and doable with Spirit:2 (in that case, the mage called upon an angel of light to illuminate the area by causing the torches to alight). Note, of course, that many spirits don't always respond with haste, even when local, which is why many Spirit Talkers often have &quot;x&quot; arrangements with various spirits set up in advance and maintained over time (via multiple rolls and/or assigned successes). Spirit:3 can rouse a lulled spirit to do &quot;x&quot; when they may be local but otherwise dormant; Spirit:4 allows those who can't normally do so to manifest and perform &quot;x&quot;. The balance, again, wherein Spirit doesn't boss-out the other Spheres is the nature of spirits, themselves: most such Effects aren't done via Fast Casting or even within a given turn -- they take time to sway/cajole/intimidate a given spirit (or group of spirits) to perform &quot;x&quot;, and thus a Forces and or Prime/what-have-you Effect would be more effective in the short term (and often long term, if a mage doesn't want to have to permanently bind a spirit to an object or into service). Also, to re-stress, this isn't a case of Spirit causing &quot;x&quot; to happen, directly, but rather it compelling a spirit to use *its* innate powers/charms/et al to perform &quot;x&quot;. Often enough, a given mage may find that there is no spirit available to do &quot;x&quot; in a given area or situation. That makes Spirit less reliable than Forces/whatnot to perform &quot;x&quot; with any reliability.<br /> <br /> The devil is in the details...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}